IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc21-nouns.l4 -- the nouns of Parts XVII to XIX (ss 530 to 572) that more than one of this part's modules use: DECLAREs, plus the three small
-- three-valued helpers (a MAYBE BOOLEAN combined the way the text's "and", "or" and "not" carry an unanswered case through).
-- Written for part ccc21. Every top-level name, every type and every constructor begins with the label of the provision that introduces it.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); not the official text.
-- The membership test used: could a witness of ordinary competence testify to the fact (what the accused answered when put to an election, what the offence charged is,
-- how much the property is alleged to be worth), or does answering it require reading the Act? Only the first kind is here.

§ `Mode of trial and the accused's answer (section 536(2))`

-- 536 (2) ... "You have the option to elect to be tried by a provincial court judge without a jury; or you may elect to be tried by a judge without a jury; or you may elect to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury."
-- src:11887 | You have the option to elect to be tried by a provincial court judge without a jury and without having had a preliminary inquiry; or you may elect to be tried by a judge without a jury; or you may elect to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury. If you do not elect now, you are deemed to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury. If you elect to be tried by a judge without a jury or by a court composed of a judge and jury or if you are deemed to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury, you will have a preliminary inquiry only if you or the prosecutor requests one. How do you elect to be tried?
@ref s 536(2) (src:11887-11887)
DECLARE `s 536(2) mode of trial` IS ONE OF
    `s 536(2) trial by a provincial court judge`
    `s 536(2) trial by a judge without a jury`
    `s 536(2) trial by a court composed of a judge and jury`

-- What the accused says when put to an election: "elects" a mode, or "does not elect".
-- src:11887 | You have the option to elect to be tried by a provincial court judge without a jury and without having had a preliminary inquiry; or you may elect to be tried by a judge without a jury; or you may elect to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury. If you do not elect now, you are deemed to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury. If you elect to be tried by a judge without a jury or by a court composed of a judge and jury or if you are deemed to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury, you will have a preliminary inquiry only if you or the prosecutor requests one. How do you elect to be tried?
@ref s 536(2) (src:11887-11887)
DECLARE `s 536(2) the accused's answer when put to an election` IS ONE OF
    `s 536(2) elects` HAS `s 536(2) the mode elected` IS A `s 536(2) mode of trial`
    `s 536(2) does not elect`

§ `The charge, for the purposes of Parts XVIII and XIX (sections 535 and 553)`

-- 553 (a) (i) theft, other than theft of cattle, (ii) obtaining money or property by false pretences, (iii) unlawfully having in his possession any property or thing or any proceeds ... obtained by or derived from an offence punishable by indictment,
-- (iv) having, by deceit, falsehood or other fraudulent means, defrauded the public or any person ... of any property, money or valuable security, or (v) mischief under subsection 430(4).
-- src:12235 | (a) with
-- src:12236 | (i) theft, other than theft of cattle,
-- src:12237 | (ii) obtaining money or property by false pretences,
-- src:12238 | (iii) unlawfully having in his possession any property or thing or any proceeds of any property or thing knowing that all or a part of the property or thing or of the proceeds was obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from the commission in Canada of an offence punishable by indictment or an act or omission anywhere that, if it had occurred in Canada, would have constituted an offence punishable by indictment,
-- src:12239 | (iv) having, by deceit, falsehood or other fraudulent means, defrauded the public or any person, whether ascertained or not, of any property, money or valuable security, or
-- src:12240 | (v) mischief under subsection 430(4),
@ref s 553(a) (src:12235-12240)
DECLARE `s 553(a) the offence charged, as paragraph (a) names it` IS ONE OF
    `s 553(a)(i) theft`
    `s 553(a)(ii) obtaining money or property by false pretences`
    `s 553(a)(iii) unlawfully having in possession property or a thing, or the proceeds of it, obtained by or derived from an offence punishable by indictment`
    `s 553(a)(iv) defrauding the public or any person of any property, money or valuable security by deceit, falsehood or other fraudulent means`
    `s 553(a)(v) mischief under subsection 430(4)`
    `s 553(a) an offence that paragraph (a) does not name`

-- 553 (b) with counselling or with a conspiracy or attempt to commit or with being an accessory after the fact to the commission of (i) any offence referred to in paragraph (a) ..., or (ii) any offence referred to in paragraph (c).
-- src:12242 | (b) with counselling or with a conspiracy or attempt to commit or with being an accessory after the fact to the commission of
-- src:12243 | (i) any offence referred to in paragraph (a) in respect of the subject-matter and value thereof referred to in that paragraph, or
-- src:12244 | (ii) any offence referred to in paragraph (c); or
@ref s 553(b) (src:12242-12244)
DECLARE `s 553(b) how the accused is charged` IS ONE OF
    `s 553(b) with the offence itself`
    `s 553(b) with counselling the offence`
    `s 553(b) with a conspiracy to commit the offence`
    `s 553(b) with an attempt to commit the offence`
    `s 553(b) with being an accessory after the fact to the commission of the offence`

